== 11. Error in the Judgment

The eleventh device that Satan has to draw the soul to sin is by polluting and defiling the souls and judgments of men with dangerous errors, errors whose own tendency is to carry the souls of men to all looseness and wickedness, as woeful experience abundantly shows. Ah, how many are filled with these and similar Christ-dishonoring and soul-ruining opinions! Namely: That ordinances are poor, low, carnal things, and are not only to be lived above, but lived without also. That the Scriptures are full of fallacies and uncertainties, and are to be heeded no further than they agree with the spirit that is in men. That it is a poor, low thing, if not idolatry too, to worship God in a Mediator. That the resurrection is already past. That there was never any such man or person as Jesus Christ, but that it is all an #emph[allegory,] and signifies nothing but light and love and such good frames born in men. That there is no God, nor devil, heaven, nor hell, except what is within us. That there is no sin in the saints, and they are under no law but that of the spirit, which is all freedom. That sin and grace are equally from God and agree with his will. With a hundred other horrid opinions, which have made wickedness break in like a flood among us, etc.

#strong[Now the general remedies against this device of Satan are as follows.]

The first remedy against this device of Satan is solemnly to consider that an erroneous, vain mind is as hateful#footnote[A blind eye is worse than a lame foot. Lev 13:44.] to God as a life of vice. He who had the leprosy in his head was to be pronounced utterly unclean. Gross errors make the heart foolish, and render the life loose and the soul of little weight in the eye of God. Error spreads and eats away#footnote[The breath of the erroneous is infectious, and like the dogs of Congo, they bite though they do not bark.] like gangrene, and makes the soul a leper in the sight of God. It was God’s heavy and dreadful plague on the Gentiles to be given up to a mind void of judgment, or an undiscerning mind, or a mind rejected, disallowed and abhorred by God, or a mind that no one has cause to glory in, but rather to be ashamed#footnote[To persist in error out of stubbornness is devilish. Best of all would be never to err; next to that, to amend our error.] of. I think that in these days God punishes many men’s former wickedness by giving them up to soul-ruining errors. Ah Lord! This mercy I humbly beg: that you would rather take me into your own hand and do anything with me than give me up to those sad errors to which thousands have married their souls, and so are in the way of perishing forever.

The second remedy against this device of Satan is to receive the truth affectionately, and let it dwell in your#super[+] souls richly. When men stand out against the truth, when truth would enter#footnote[The greatest sinners are sure to be the greatest sufferers.] and men bar the door of their souls against it, God in justice gives up such souls to be deluded and deceived by error, to their eternal ruin. 2 Thess 2:10, 11, 12: “Because they did not receive the love of the truth that would have saved them, … God will send them a powerful delusion”#footnote[ἐνέργειαν πλάνης.] (or as the Greek has it, the efficacy of error) “so that they believe a lie, in order that all may be damned who have disbelieved the truth and delighted in wickedness.” Ah, sirs! As you#super[+] love your#super[+] souls, do not tempt God; do not provoke God, by your#super[+] withstanding truth and outfacing truth, to give you#super[+] up to believe a lie, that you#super[+] may be damned. There are no men on earth so fenced against error as those who receive the truth in the love of it. Such souls#footnote[Eph 4:14: ἐν τῇ κυβείᾳ. The Greek means cheating with loaded dice: such sleights as cheats and crooked gamblers use at dice.] are not easily “tossed about … and carried around by every wind of teaching, by the sleight of men and the cunning craftiness of their deceitful scheming.” It is not he who receives most of the truth into his head, but he who receives most of the truth affectionately into his heart, who will enjoy the happiness of having his judgment sound and clear when others are deluded and deceived by those who make it their business to infect the judgments and ruin the souls of men.

Ah, souls! If you#super[+] would not have your#super[+] judgments polluted and defiled#footnote[Col 3:16: ἐνοικείτω, that is, let it dwell in you#super[+] as an implanted word, built into your#super[+] souls, so taken in and digested by you#super[+] that you#super[+] turn it into a part of yourselves#super[+]. Those who do not know God’s ways must err; yet they cannot wander so far astray as to miss hell. #emph[Veritas vincit:] truth (at last) triumphs.] with error, let the word of the Lord, which is more precious than gold, indeed than fine gold, dwell richly in you#super[+]. It is not the hearing of truth, nor the knowing of truth, nor the commending of truth, nor the talking of truth, but the indwelling of truth in your#super[+] souls that will keep your#super[+] judgments chaste and sound in the midst of all those glittering errors. Those errors betray many souls into the hands of him who can easily “masquerade as an angel of light,” so that he may draw others to lie in chains of darkness with him forever. Oh, do not let the word be a stranger, but make it your#super[+] choicest companion! Then you#super[+] will be able to stand in the day when many fall on your#super[+] right hand and on your#super[+] left by the cunning of those who say, “Look, here is Christ,” and “Look, there is Christ.” There was more cleverness than grace in the saying of the man who advised his friend not to come too near to truth, lest its heels kick out his teeth. Ah, souls! If truth dwells richly in#footnote[#emph[Veritas stat in aperto campo.] Truth stands in the open fields; yes, and it makes those souls stand in whom it dwells, when others fall like stars from heaven.] you#super[+], you#super[+] are happy; if not, you#super[+] are unhappy in all your#super[+] greatest good fortune. “It is with truth,” says Melanchthon, “as it is with holy water. Everyone praises it and thinks it has some rare power in it; but offer to sprinkle them with it, and they will shut their eyes and turn their faces away from it.”

The third remedy against this device of Satan is solemnly to consider that error makes its owner suffer loss. All the pains and labor that men take to defend and maintain their errors, to spread them abroad and infect the world with them, will bring them no profit and no comfort in that day when “each man’s#footnote[Error, like glass, is bright but brittle, and cannot endure the hammer or the fire, as gold can, which, though rubbed or melted, remains firm and lustrous.] work will be made evident, and the fire will test its quality,” as the apostle shows in that remarkable Scripture, 1 Cor 3:11, 12, 13, 14, 15. Ah, that all those who rise early and go to bed late, who spend their time, their strength, their spirits, their all, to advance and spread abroad God-dishonoring and soul-ruining opinions, would seriously consider this: that they will lose all the pains, cost and expense that they have spent or will spend for the propagating of error; and if they are ever saved, it will be by fire, as the apostle shows there. Ah, sirs! Is it nothing to lay out your#super[+] money for that which is not bread, and your#super[+] strength for that which will not, which cannot, profit you#super[+] in the day when you#super[+] must settle your#super[+] accounts and all your#super[+] works must be tested by fire? Ah, that such souls would now at last buy the truth and not sell it! Remember, you#super[+] can never pay too much for it, whatever you#super[+] give for it; you#super[+] can never sell it at its worth, even if you#super[+] had all the world in exchange for it. It is said of Caesar#footnote[Major fuit cura Caesari libellorum quam purpurae.] that he took greater care of his books than of his royal robes; for when he swam through the waters to escape his enemies, he carried his books in his hand above the water, but lost his robes. Ah, what are Caesar’s books to God’s books? Well, remember this: one day, indeed one hour, spent in the pursuit of truth or the spreading abroad of truth will yield the soul more comfort and profit than many thousand years spent in the pursuit and spreading abroad of corrupt and vain opinions that have their rise from hell and not from heaven, from the god of this world and not from that God who will at last judge this world and all the corrupt opinions of men.

The fourth #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to hate, reject and abhor all those doctrines and opinions that are contrary to godliness and that open a door to profaneness;#footnote[One old piece of gold is worth a thousand new counters, and one old truth of God is worth more than a thousand new errors. True hatred is (εἰς τὰ γένη) against the whole kind: it is sad to frown on one error and smile on another. Gideon had seventy sons and only one bastard, and yet that bastard destroyed all the rest. Judg 8:30, 31; 9:5. One wrong turn may bring a man quite out of the way.] and all such doctrines and opinions as require men to hold out a strictness beyond what the Scripture requires; and all such doctrines and opinions as advance and lift up corrupted nature to the doing of supernatural things, which none can do except by that supernatural power that raised Christ from the grave; and all such opinions as lift up our own righteousness in the place of Christ’s righteousness, that put good works on the throne of Christ and make them co-partners with Christ, etc.; and all those opinions and doctrines that so set up and cry up Christ and his righteousness as to cry down all duties of holiness and righteousness; and all those doctrines and opinions that make the glorious and blessed privileges of believers in the days of the gospel less, fewer and weaker than they were in the time of the law. Ah, if your#super[+] souls rose up with a holy hatred and a strong indignation against such doctrines and opinions, you#super[+] would stand when others fall, and you#super[+] would shine like the sun in her glory, when many who were once like shining stars may go out like stinking candle-ends.

The fifth #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to hold fast the truth. As men take no hold on the arm of flesh till they have let go their hold on#footnote[Jer 17:5.] the arm of God, so men take no hold on error till they have let go their hold on truth. Therefore hold fast the truth. Truth is your crown; hold fast your crown, and let no man take your crown from you. Has not God made#footnote[2 Tim 1:13. Titus 1:9. The priests of Mercury, when they ate their figs and honey, cried out (γλυκὺ ἡ ἀλήθεια), “Sweet is truth.”] truth sweet to your soul, indeed “sweeter than honey, than the honeycomb”? And will you not go on to heaven feeding on truth, that heavenly honeycomb, as Samson fed on his honeycomb? Ah, souls! Have you#super[+] not found truth sweetening your#super[+] spirits, and cheering your#super[+] spirits, and warming your#super[+] spirits, and raising your#super[+] spirits, and strengthening your#super[+] spirits? Have you#super[+] not found truth a guide to lead you#super[+], a staff to uphold you#super[+], a heart-medicine to strengthen you#super[+], and a plaster to heal you#super[+]? And will you#super[+] not hold fast the truth? Has not truth been your#super[+] best friend in your#super[+] worst days? Has not truth stood by you#super[+] when friends have forsaken you#super[+]? Has not truth done more for you#super[+] than all the world could do against you#super[+], and will you#super[+] not hold fast the truth? Is not truth your#super[+] right eye, without which you#super[+] cannot see for Christ? And your#super[+] right hand, without which you#super[+] cannot do anything for Christ? And your#super[+] right foot, without which you#super[+] cannot walk with Christ? And will you#super[+] not hold fast truth? Oh, hold fast the truth in your#super[+] judgments and understandings, in your#super[+] wills and affections, in your#super[+] profession of faith#footnote[It is with truth as with some plants, which live and thrive only in warm climates.] and conduct! Truth is more precious than gold or rubies, and all the things you can desire are not to be compared with her. Truth is that heavenly mirror in which we may see the luster and glory of divine wisdom, power, greatness, love and mercifulness. In this mirror you#super[+] may see the face of Christ, the favor of Christ, the riches of Christ, and the heart of Christ beating and working sweetly toward your#super[+] souls. Oh, let your#super[+] souls cling to truth as Ruth#footnote[Ruth 1:15, 16, 17. “Though I cannot dispute for the truth, yet I can die for the truth,” said that blessed martyr.] did to Naomi, and say, “I will not leave #emph[truth] or turn back from following after #emph[truth.] Wherever #emph[truth] goes, I will go, and wherever #emph[truth] lodges, I will lodge, and nothing but death shall part #emph[truth] and my soul.” What John said to the church of Philadelphia I may say to you#super[+]: “Hold fast to what you have, so that no one will take your crown.” The crown is the top of royalties; such a thing is truth. Let#footnote[Titus 1:9. Ἀντεχόμενον \[holding fast\].] no man take your crown. “Hold fast to the faithful word,” as Titus speaks. You#super[+] had better let go anything than truth. You#super[+] had better let go your#super[+]#footnote[Hold it fast as with tooth and nail, against those who would snatch it from us.] honors and riches, your#super[+] friends and pleasures, and the world’s favors, indeed your#super[+] nearest and dearest relations, yes, your#super[+] very lives, than let go truth. Oh, keep the truth, and truth will keep you#super[+] safe and happy for#footnote[I have read of one who, seeing in a vision many snares of the devil spread on the earth, sat down mourning and said within himself (#emph[Quis pertransiet ista]), “Who shall pass through these?” And he heard a voice answering (#emph[humilitas pertransiet]), “Humility shall pass through them.”] ever! Blessed are those souls that are kept by truth.

The sixth #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is to keep humble. Humility will keep the soul free from many darts of Satan’s casting and erroneous snares of his spreading. As low trees and shrubs are free from many violent gusts and blasts of wind that shake and tear the taller trees, so humble souls are free from those gusts and blasts of error that tear and rend proud, lofty souls. Satan and the world have least power to fasten errors on humble souls. The God of light and truth delights to dwell with the humble; and the more light and truth dwell in the soul, the further off darkness and error will stand from the soul. The God of grace pours grace into humble souls as men pour liquid into empty vessels; and the more grace is poured into the soul, the less error will be able to overpower the soul or to infect it. That is a sweet word in#footnote[Ps 25:9. ענוים #emph[Gnanavim,] from ענה #emph[gnanah,] which signifies the humble, or afflicted. The high tide quickly ebbs, and the highest sun is soon declining; you#super[+] know how to apply it.] Ps 25:9: “He guides the meek” (or the humble) “in judgment and teaches the meek His way.” And certainly souls guided by God and taught by God are not easily drawn aside into ways of error. Oh, beware of spiritual pride! Pride fills our fancies, and weakens our graces, and makes room in our hearts for error. There are no men on earth so soon entangled and so easily conquered by error as proud souls. Oh, it is dangerous to love to be wise above what is written; to be overcurious and unsober in your#super[+] desire for knowledge; to#footnote[The proud soul is like the man who gazed at the moon but fell into the pit.] trust to your#super[+] own capacities and abilities; to undertake to pry into all secrets; and to be puffed up by a carnal mind! Souls that are soaring up in this way above the bounds and limits of humility usually fall into the very worst of errors, as experience daily shows.

The seventh #emph[remedy] against this device of Satan is solemnly to consider the great evils that errors have produced. Error is a fruitful mother, and has brought forth such monstrous#footnote[Errors in conscience produce many great evils, not only (#emph[ad intra]) within men’s own souls, but also (#emph[ad extra]) in human affairs.] children as have set towns, cities and nations on fire. Error is that whorish woman who has cast down many, wounded many, indeed slain many strong men, and many great men, and many learned men, and many professing men, in former times and in our own time, as is all too evident to all who are not much forsaken by God, destitute of the truth, and blinded by Satan. Oh, the graces that error has weakened, and the sweet joys and comforts that error has clouded, if not buried! Oh, the hands that error has weakened, the eyes that error has blinded, the judgments of men that error has perverted, the minds that error has darkened, the hearts that error has hardened, the affections that error has cooled, the consciences that error has seared, and the lives of men that error has polluted! Ah, souls! Can you#super[+] solemnly consider this and not tremble more at error than at hell itself? etc.
